(7732039, 1273830, 113411, '<td valign="top">Great shot, Anita!</td>', 'Great shot, Anita!', '2022-11-03 14:48:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7734889, 1273685, 29535, '<td valign="top">Hi Rucl1124!<br/> <br/>Good job on nailing the challenge topic, this is often the trickiest part.<br/> <br/>I''m not sure what camera you''re using but it looks like it was struggling for light. For cats especially they look much better than people do when the sun is relatively strong, this will help with the noise/grain on your image.<br/> <br/>And if possible, try for a composition where they are far from their background, to enable it to be blurred out and isolate them in frame.<br/> <br/>Good luck and welcome to DPC!</td>', 'Hi Rucl1124! Good job on nailing the challenge topic, this is often the trickiest part. I''m not sure what camera you''re using but it looks like it was struggling for light. For cats especially they look much better than people do when the sun is relatively strong, this will help with the noise/grain on your image. And if possible, try for a composition where they are far from their background, to enable it to be blurred out and isolate them in frame. Good luck and welcome to DPC!', '2022-12-18 13:14:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7734891, 1273738, 29535, '<td valign="top">I actually think this is a good choice of subject and a well exposed/composed photo with just two major things letting it down - the finger in the bottom left and the crooked horizon!<br/> <br/>Don''t give up, I look forward to seeing you in future contests. For what it''s worth I think this would have gotten at least a 6 fixing these two minor issues so be careful next time!</td>', 'I actually think this is a good choice of subject and a well exposed/composed photo with just two major things letting it down - the finger in the bottom left and the crooked horizon! Don''t give up, I look forward to seeing you in future contests. For what it''s worth I think this would have gotten at least a 6 fixing these two minor issues so be careful next time!', '2022-12-18 13:19:06.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
